00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.660
The biggest barrier to
enterprise data analysis

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.630
and machine learning
is data integration.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.390
It is not uncommon to
see companies struggle

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.430
to get their data in one place,
move it around, transform

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.450
it, and make sense out of it.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.590
Because honestly, it's a
really hard problem to solve.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.400
Cloud Data Fusion is a
fully-managed, cloud-native

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.990
data integration service that
helps users efficiently build

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.430
and manage data pipelines.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:52.590
With a graphical interface and
a broad open sourced library

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.860
of preconfigured connectors
and transformations,

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.040
Data Fusion shifts an
organization's focus

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.390
away from code and integration
to insights and action.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.500
Data Fusion is built on the
open-source project CDAP.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.420
And this open core ensures data
pipeline portability for users.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.590
Data Fusion aims at making the
lives of data practitioners

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.240
easier by providing a graphical
user interface to visually

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.090
drag and drop elements
to create data pipelines,

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.810
and then finally run it on GCP.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:31.380
In Data Fusion, we collect
metadata information

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.530
on fields and tables, and
expose them as lineage,

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:39.540
so you can do root cause
analysis and impact analysis.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.080
Data Fusion can solve
a variety of use cases.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.290
If you're building a data
warehouse using BigQuery,

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.300
you should look at
Data Fusion, since it

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.180
can connect to multiple
different data sources,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:56.400
like Oracle and other relational
and non-relational databases.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.310
If you're looking to
retire a legacy system,

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.330
Data Fusion can help you
migrate the data to GCP.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.730
If you're looking
to consolidate data,

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.340
or in a hybrid
environment, you can

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.039
use Data Fusion for
data consistency

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:14.910
across cloud and
on-premise environment.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.210
Data Fusion natively
integrates with Google Cloud,

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.940
which simplifies data
security and ensures

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.450
your data is immediately
available for analysis.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.050
Data Fusion offers both
preconfigured transformations

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:32.020
from an OSS library
as well as the ability

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.800
to create an internal
library of custom connections

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.030
and transformations that can be
validated, shared, and reused

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:42.740
across an organization.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:46.400
It lays the foundation of
collaborative data engineering

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.100
and improves productivity.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:53.180
This means less waiting for
data engineers, and importantly,

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.670
less sweating
about code quality.

